# mudi-volte: let the operator's IMS core reach the VoLTE client.
# The IMS connection (rmnet_dataN) belongs to no fw4 zone, so without these
# rules inbound calls are rejected once the conntrack entry of our own traffic
# expires (about 200 s of quiet). ESP carries the protected SIP; after the
# kernel decrypts it, new TCP connections from the P-CSCF re-enter this chain
# in clear and are recognised by their IPsec origin. The interface number of
# the internet and the IMS connection can swap, so every rmnet_data* matches;
# ESP to the internet address finds no security association and is dropped.
iifname "rmnet_data*" meta l4proto esp counter accept comment "mudi-volte: IMS ESP in"
iifname "rmnet_data*" meta ipsec exists counter accept comment "mudi-volte: IMS IPsec in"
